      "text": "Fluconazole (Diflucan) label:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " OPC in pts ≥ 6 mo: 6 mg/kg on the first day, then 3 mg/kg once daily; treat ≥ 2 wks to ↓ relapse."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "CI: hypersensitivity to fluconazole or excipients; QT-prolonging CYP3A4 substrates (eg, erythromycin, pimozide, quinidine). Caution in liver dysfun: rare serious hepatotoxicity, incl deaths (mainly in pts w serious underlying dz). Rare QT prolongation and torsades reported; hypokalemia and advanced HF ↑ the risk of life-threatening ventricular arrhythmias; ⍉ combine w erythromycin (cardiotoxicity, sudden death)."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
